WEBVTT

00:02:00.310 --> 00:02:05.180
Yes, we just arrived at the station.
We're about to pass the general admission queue.

00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:07.880
Madarame-san, are you guys in line, too?

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:10.930
<i>Yeah, we're at the front, more or less.</i>

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:12.820
<i>Can you see us?</i>

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:15.140
No, we can't.

00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:17.490
<i>I see. It shouldn't come as a surprise.</i>

00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:20.160
<i>You're going to shop around first, right?</i>

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:24.840
Yeah.
We'll arrive at the booth around noon.

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:25.940
<i>Got it.</i>

00:02:25.940 --> 00:02:28.960
Tanaka and Ohno-san will head over
there as soon as Ohno finishes changing.

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:32.130
Could you also tell Kuchiki-kun to take care
of the more popular vendors?

00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:34.850
Okay, I'll see you later.

00:02:34.850 --> 00:02:37.550
Kuchiki-kun, they want you to take care of the popular vendors.

00:02:40.630 --> 00:02:41.760
Plebeians!

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:43.390
Now, now.

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:45.270
We're not doing anything right now.

00:02:45.270 --> 00:02:46.820
I'm fully aware of that.

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:51.810
Today's mission is to line up at the
vendor queues before opening hours,

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:56.960
enter the venue as a circle participant and
stand in the lines of the well-known vendors,

00:02:56.960 --> 00:03:01.580
and make sure to purchase their new
titles before the general audience does!

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:06.250
It's a dirty job, one that's suited for someone like me!

00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:09.560
You shouldn't say that out loud.

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:12.130
Well, everyone knows about it.

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:21.970
Wow, there are hardly any people!

00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:24.720
Is that the preliminary line?

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:26.370
Is that what it is?

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:30.280
I see. They gather everybody here and escort them outside.

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:34.710
If they gather everybody inside, there's no telling
what would happen due to the sheer number of people.

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:38.330
Should I get in line, too?

00:03:38.330 --> 00:03:39.360
Are you really going to?

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:41.410
I'm off!

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:47.030
This is it.

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:48.250
Our book's already here.

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:50.750
We have to go all the way around to get inside.

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:52.170
Y-Yeah.

00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:55.730
Wow, that's a lot of flyers.

00:03:55.730 --> 00:03:57.130
Good morning!

00:03:57.130 --> 00:03:58.260
Nice to be here with you.

00:03:58.260 --> 00:03:59.940
Oh, likewise.

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:02.880
Nice to...

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:06.380
S-Should I open it?

00:04:06.380 --> 00:04:08.590
Of course. Let's see it!

00:04:16.930 --> 00:04:19.810
The quality is great.
There aren't any printing flaws.

00:04:19.810 --> 00:04:21.660
<i>Thanks, printing company employees!</i>

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:24.280
We were supposed to keep twenty copies for ourselves, right?

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:25.270
Let's set those aside now.

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:29.440
We also need to put a sample sticker on the display book.

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:31.270
Oh, good morning!

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:33.090
Good morning.

00:04:33.090 --> 00:04:35.270
Let's start setting things up.

00:04:35.270 --> 00:04:36.290
Sure.

00:04:46.270 --> 00:04:47.720
How is it?

00:04:48.230 --> 00:04:49.750
Looks good.

00:04:49.750 --> 00:04:53.360
Using point of purchase displays really makes a difference.

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:56.150
Everyone sure is putting a lot of effort into it.

00:04:56.660 --> 00:04:58.680
<i>Our neighbor's also selling a book about the president.</i>

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:01.720
<i>I guess it can't be helped,
considering how popular Kujiun is around here.</i>

00:05:01.720 --> 00:05:02.580
Hey.

00:05:02.580 --> 00:05:03.780
Oh, Takayanagi-san.

00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:06.190
Oh, you finished after all.

00:05:06.190 --> 00:05:07.340
Great.

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:08.160
It's thanks to you.

00:05:08.930 --> 00:05:12.180
Here, have a copy of our new book.

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:13.960
Oh, from the Manga Club?

00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:15.900
Here's one of ours in return.

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:16.870
Thanks.

00:05:17.230 --> 00:05:19.920
Haraguuro's here, so be on your guard.

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:23.110
Did he enter with a ticket from the Manga Club?

00:05:23.110 --> 00:05:27.330
No, it looks like he got it from one of
the more popular circles or something.

00:05:27.330 --> 00:05:32.220
Established vendors require a lot of people,
so they're able to make requests for more tickets.

00:05:33.730 --> 00:05:36.980
In any case, there's not much you can do about him.

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:41.030
Well, knowing if he's here or not makes a big difference.

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:44.340
Well, take it easy.

00:05:44.340 --> 00:05:45.570
Thanks.

00:05:47.590 --> 00:05:49.820
Haraguuro's here, huh? What are we going to do?

00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:52.240
Well, he's already here.

00:05:52.580 --> 00:05:54.750
Hey, what's up?

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:57.420
He's really light on his feet for a guy his size.

00:05:57.790 --> 00:06:00.460
So you've come up with a new book, huh?

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:01.920
Please take a look...

00:06:03.520 --> 00:06:05.300
You can have one for free.

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:08.220
Well, I think I'll pass.

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:09.850
<i>This guy...</i>

00:06:09.850 --> 00:06:11.290
Well, break a leg.

00:06:11.290 --> 00:06:13.440
I hope you sell everything.

00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:19.070
He sure knows how to jinx people.

00:06:19.740 --> 00:06:22.460
Well, it'd be great if we actually sold everything.

00:06:22.460 --> 00:06:23.140
Did you say something?

00:06:23.140 --> 00:06:23.650
No.

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:40.310
Thank you for your patience. We will now officially
commence the third day of the sixty-sixth Comic Festival.

00:06:41.110 --> 00:06:42.170
<i>It's started.</i>

00:06:42.170 --> 00:06:44.150
Wow. Is the ground shaking?

00:06:44.150 --> 00:06:49.910
Oh, could it be the sound of the dash from the opening gate?

00:06:49.910 --> 00:06:52.640
Aren't you glad we're not
in front of a large aisle?

00:07:05.460 --> 00:07:07.280
<i>He's looking at us, he's looking at us...</i>

00:07:07.720 --> 00:07:09.350
Mind if I take a look?

00:07:09.350 --> 00:07:10.130
Sure.

00:07:10.130 --> 00:07:11.240
Please do!

00:07:14.140 --> 00:07:15.410
I'll take it.

00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:18.040
Th-Thank you very much.

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:19.870
That'll be five hundred yen.

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:21.300
Here's a thousand.

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:25.020
Y-Your change comes out to five hundred yen...

00:07:25.020 --> 00:07:26.870
Thank you very much!

00:07:26.870 --> 00:07:28.190
It sold!

00:07:28.190 --> 00:07:28.810
It really did.

00:07:33.510 --> 00:07:36.970
<i>Come on... One more... Come on... One more...</i>

00:07:38.990 --> 00:07:41.320
Selling the next copy sure is difficult.

00:07:42.890 --> 00:07:45.810
I have an idea. Why don't we stand up?

00:07:46.980 --> 00:07:50.980
I think it'll be easier on us and the customers.

00:07:50.980 --> 00:07:53.210
We should also specialize our tasks.

00:07:53.890 --> 00:07:57.140
I'll be in charge of receiving the money and handling the book,

00:07:57.140 --> 00:07:59.670
while you take care of
the change, Sasahara-kun.

00:07:59.670 --> 00:08:01.020
I see.

00:08:01.020 --> 00:08:02.790
Please feel free to look!

00:08:02.790 --> 00:08:07.380
<i>Yeah, it was a good idea to bring Kousaka-kun along.</i>

00:08:07.890 --> 00:08:10.910
<i>Wow, someone's already here.</i>

00:08:10.910 --> 00:08:12.550
Please take a look.

00:08:14.510 --> 00:08:17.430
<i>If he pays with a thousand yen bill,
I'll have to give him a five hundred yen coin.</i>

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:18.430
Thanks.

00:08:19.610 --> 00:08:21.100
Thank you very much!

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:25.080
Isn't it frustrating when people
stop to look but don't buy anything?

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:27.880
We do that all the time.

00:08:27.880 --> 00:08:29.530
Yeah, you're right.

00:08:35.820 --> 00:08:38.690
<i>The ensuing battle was like a tug-of-war.</i>

00:08:38.690 --> 00:08:42.870
<i>Sometimes there'd be plenty of sales,
and sometimes there wouldn't be any business at all.</i>

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:44.830
<i>Total copies sold: twenty.</i>

00:08:46.950 --> 00:08:50.340
<i>That might be good for a first time participant,</i>

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:54.400
<i>but at this rate, selling everything might be unrealistic.</i>

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:56.400
I hope you sell everything.

00:08:56.400 --> 00:08:57.950
<i>No way, no way.</i>

00:09:00.920 --> 00:09:03.890
Oh, wow! They're really doing it!

00:09:04.230 --> 00:09:07.520
Ohno-san's ceremonial version of the vice president!

00:09:07.840 --> 00:09:09.430
It's a Kujiun book, after all.

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:11.780
I'll be a vendor.

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:13.530
You can take my place.

00:09:14.270 --> 00:09:15.320
Why?

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:19.110
It would be more appealing to receive a book from a girl, right?

00:09:20.440 --> 00:09:23.300
Besides, there's something that Tanaka-san and I need to do.

00:09:23.300 --> 00:09:23.870
Is that so?

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:26.030
I'll be back in a little while.

00:09:26.030 --> 00:09:27.430
Good luck.

00:09:27.430 --> 00:09:28.280
What is it?

00:09:28.280 --> 00:09:29.540
It's a secret.

00:09:29.540 --> 00:09:31.570
I have a bad feeling about this.

00:09:31.570 --> 00:09:34.010
Please take a look.

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:35.800
I'd like one.

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:37.060
Thank you very much.

00:09:37.060 --> 00:09:38.330
That'll be five hundred yen.

00:09:38.330 --> 00:09:39.390
Here, too.

00:09:39.390 --> 00:09:40.310
Five hundred yen.

00:09:40.310 --> 00:09:42.010
Here's your change.

00:09:42.010 --> 00:09:43.840
Thank you very much.

00:09:43.840 --> 00:09:44.140
Here's your change. Thanks.

00:09:44.140 --> 00:09:47.250
<i>Wow, sales are really taking off.</i>

00:09:47.250 --> 00:09:50.810
<i>Isn't she embarrassed to be in costume as a female vendor?</i>

00:09:50.810 --> 00:09:52.640
<i>Couldn't that be considered sexual harassment?</i>

00:09:52.640 --> 00:09:53.060
Thank you very much.

00:09:53.060 --> 00:09:55.070
<i>It seems like she's enjoying it.</i>

00:09:55.070 --> 00:09:56.960
Please take a look at it.

00:09:57.760 --> 00:09:59.530
<i>She's not only bold. It's like she was born to do this.</i>

00:10:00.260 --> 00:10:02.130
Thank you very much!

00:10:11.300 --> 00:10:12.880
Hey!

00:10:13.480 --> 00:10:15.320
Hey, you're early.

00:10:15.320 --> 00:10:16.840
Well, you had me concerned.

00:10:17.290 --> 00:10:18.760
Just the two of you?

00:10:19.280 --> 00:10:22.150
Kousaka-kun and Tanaka-san went somewhere together.

00:10:22.150 --> 00:10:23.670
I wonder where!

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:26.210
How's it going?

00:10:26.210 --> 00:10:28.000
Not bad at all,

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:30.110
but we haven't sold half yet.

00:10:30.110 --> 00:10:31.620
Think we'll sell out?

00:10:31.620 --> 00:10:34.150
It'd be better not to ask.

00:10:34.650 --> 00:10:36.700
Do you want me to take
your place, Sasahara?

00:10:36.700 --> 00:10:38.540
You can take a break.

00:10:38.540 --> 00:10:39.200
Really?

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:42.920
I wanted to be a vendor
for a change, anyway.

00:10:43.680 --> 00:10:46.010
Is it all right if I look around for a while?

00:10:46.010 --> 00:10:48.040
Yeah, sure. Go ahead.

00:10:55.730 --> 00:11:01.340
<i>For some reason, it feels great to wander
around the Comifes without having to carry anything.</i>

00:11:07.230 --> 00:11:09.520
What happened to Madarame-san?

00:11:10.220 --> 00:11:11.290
He said he had to go to the bathroom.

00:11:11.290 --> 00:11:12.380
That's his story.

00:11:12.380 --> 00:11:13.980
<i>He ran away, didn't he?</i>

00:11:39.010 --> 00:11:40.170
Now...

00:11:40.170 --> 00:11:43.620
I wonder how Kuchiki-kun is doing.

00:11:43.620 --> 00:11:45.850
I hope he's not stuck in a loop.

00:11:45.850 --> 00:11:46.510
Loop?

00:11:46.890 --> 00:11:52.070
Once you start buying this and that,
this strange kind of adrenaline starts flowing out.

00:11:56.060 --> 00:12:01.970
Why is it when you're a vendor,
you don't feel a need to buy anything?

00:12:01.970 --> 00:12:03.970
Oh, you're right.

00:12:03.970 --> 00:12:08.370
As a general visitor, you feel obliged to
buy something as proof of your participation,

00:12:08.370 --> 00:12:13.380
but as a circle participant,
it feels like you're participating simply by being here.

00:12:14.860 --> 00:12:18.290
Well, it's partially because we have Kuchiki-kun as insurance.

00:12:18.290 --> 00:12:19.340
That's true.

00:12:22.010 --> 00:12:24.540
By the way, where's Kousaka-kun?

00:12:24.540 --> 00:12:26.000
Those two are really taking their time.

00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:30.520
You're right. That shouldn't take too much time to finish.

00:12:30.520 --> 00:12:31.730
"That"?

00:12:31.730 --> 00:12:32.480
They're back!

00:12:34.430 --> 00:12:36.590
Sorry for the wait, Chihiro-chan!

00:12:40.070 --> 00:12:43.410
W-Wait a second...

00:12:43.960 --> 00:12:46.560
It doesn't look weird at all.

00:12:46.560 --> 00:12:48.360
Why would you do this?

00:12:48.360 --> 00:12:51.160
That aside, I was right about that bad feeling.

00:12:51.160 --> 00:12:53.210
Well, it's for the occasion.

00:12:54.470 --> 00:12:56.900
It took some time to do the makeup,

00:12:56.900 --> 00:12:59.000
since I tried to imitate what Saki-chan did.

00:12:59.720 --> 00:13:00.670
<i>He's enjoying this.</i>

00:13:00.670 --> 00:13:03.030
Does Kasukabe-san know about this?

00:13:03.030 --> 00:13:04.760
There's no way I could tell her.

00:13:05.100 --> 00:13:07.050
She definitely wouldn't let me do this.

00:13:07.050 --> 00:13:08.820
May I take a look?

00:13:08.820 --> 00:13:09.680
Please!

00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:13.180
Is this when the obligatory nosebleed scene takes place?

00:13:13.180 --> 00:13:14.480
I don't think that's possible.

00:13:14.480 --> 00:13:15.850
That'll be five hundred yen!

00:13:22.240 --> 00:13:23.390
I'd like one.

00:13:23.390 --> 00:13:24.840
Five hundred yen please!

00:13:24.840 --> 00:13:26.140
Can I take a look?

00:13:26.140 --> 00:13:27.510
Thank you very much!

00:13:27.510 --> 00:13:28.420
One please.

00:13:28.420 --> 00:13:29.870
Five hundred yen please!

00:13:29.870 --> 00:13:31.370
Thank you very much!

00:13:31.370 --> 00:13:33.490
Doesn't it look like it's selling well now?

00:13:33.490 --> 00:13:36.750
Well, the book itself isn't bad.

00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:40.300
Isn't it obvious that he isn't a woman?

00:13:40.300 --> 00:13:44.010
The atmosphere in here makes that feel acceptable.

00:13:44.010 --> 00:13:45.420
It's the end of the world.

00:13:45.980 --> 00:13:48.150
Isn't it about time to open the next box?

00:13:48.150 --> 00:13:49.010
Got it.

00:13:49.010 --> 00:13:50.380
Did we sell more than a hundred?

00:13:50.380 --> 00:13:52.220
Almost, but not quite.

00:13:52.220 --> 00:13:53.430
Oh, Kugayama-san!

00:13:53.770 --> 00:13:55.630
You're late, sensei!

00:13:56.330 --> 00:14:00.150
No... Um... Kousaka-kun?

00:14:00.150 --> 00:14:01.910
It's Akiyama Tokino!

00:14:01.910 --> 00:14:02.820
Hello!

00:14:03.440 --> 00:14:06.490
Kugayama-san, go the other way and come on in.

00:14:06.490 --> 00:14:07.990
O-Okay.

00:14:11.790 --> 00:14:13.710
It's selling pretty well.

00:14:13.710 --> 00:14:15.090
I see.

00:14:15.090 --> 00:14:17.400
Much better than I expected.

00:14:17.400 --> 00:14:21.120
I-Isn't that because of these two?

00:14:21.120 --> 00:14:23.130
Well, I won't deny that,

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:25.920
but the quality's great. Here's the book.

00:14:30.290 --> 00:14:31.350
Is that all?

00:14:31.350 --> 00:14:34.570
Well, it's e-embarrassing, you know.

00:14:34.570 --> 00:14:37.280
I-I'll take a closer look later.

00:14:37.280 --> 00:14:38.620
I see.

00:14:40.860 --> 00:14:42.400
I'm glad we were able to participate.

00:14:42.720 --> 00:14:45.350
I'm glad we were able to make the book, too.

00:14:46.400 --> 00:14:47.570
Y-Yeah.

00:14:50.380 --> 00:14:52.640
Most of those circles have been placed next to the walls.

00:14:53.590 --> 00:14:55.700
Let's see. The closest one is...

00:14:57.470 --> 00:14:58.620
As expected of a popular circle.

00:14:59.180 --> 00:15:01.530
Wow, they're really stacked up.

00:15:01.530 --> 00:15:04.570
Let's say there are eighty to a hundred per box, which means there are several thousand...

00:15:04.570 --> 00:15:08.130
Come on.
You shouldn't be wasting time making estimates. Just go!

00:15:08.130 --> 00:15:09.410
Um, excuse me.

00:15:09.410 --> 00:15:12.730
Is Ihato Kouji-san here?

00:15:12.730 --> 00:15:14.290
Yes, that's me.

00:15:14.290 --> 00:15:21.560
Oh, sorry. I'm Sasahara from Shiiou University's Society for the Study of Modern Visual Culture.

00:15:21.560 --> 00:15:22.770
We've caused you a lot of trouble.

00:15:23.090 --> 00:15:24.700
Oh, you're from Genshiken.

00:15:24.700 --> 00:15:27.030
I'm really sorry about having to decline.

00:15:27.030 --> 00:15:30.840
No problem.
It was a blessing to have one less job to take care of.

00:15:30.840 --> 00:15:31.950
I-Is that so?

00:15:32.310 --> 00:15:35.620
I saw Haraguuro around here. Were you all right?

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:40.020
Well, he made some sarcastic
comments, but nothing aside from that.

00:15:40.020 --> 00:15:41.330
That's good to hear.

00:15:41.330 --> 00:15:45.190
That aside, checking out the competition is classic Haraguuro.

00:15:46.450 --> 00:15:48.040
Yeah, he stopped by before the gate opened.

00:15:48.040 --> 00:15:49.400
Oh, one second.

00:15:53.300 --> 00:15:54.920
Here, our new book.

00:15:54.920 --> 00:15:55.930
You didn't have to.

00:15:55.930 --> 00:15:58.430
In these kinds of situations,
you're supposed to graciously accept.

00:15:59.530 --> 00:16:00.530
Then...

00:16:00.530 --> 00:16:02.790
I'll bring one of ours right away.

00:16:02.790 --> 00:16:04.130
It's okay, you don't have to.

00:16:04.130 --> 00:16:05.850
There's a difference between our book's circulation levels,

00:16:05.850 --> 00:16:08.690
and it'd be a substantial number if
you were to give one to everybody.

00:16:08.980 --> 00:16:13.330
<i>I see. If I went around empty-handed,
it'd look like I was expecting free copies of new books.</i>

00:16:13.330 --> 00:16:17.430
<i>That was close. I almost came off as a rude person.</i>

00:16:30.670 --> 00:16:32.340
Good job.

00:16:32.340 --> 00:16:35.980
It seemed like there was a mountain of people and doujinshi wherever I went.

00:16:35.980 --> 00:16:38.140
I guess the popular circles are in a league of their own.

00:16:38.140 --> 00:16:40.290
Everyone was nice, though.

00:16:40.290 --> 00:16:42.780
That was probably due to the
formation of the anti-Haraguuro faction.

00:16:44.960 --> 00:16:46.440
How many do we have left?

00:16:46.440 --> 00:16:48.070
About seventy copies.

00:16:49.020 --> 00:16:52.200
Seventy, huh? I'd really like to sell all of them if possible.

00:16:52.200 --> 00:16:54.320
Yeah, I was thinking the same thing.

00:16:54.320 --> 00:16:57.820
We might as well advertise to the customers outside.

00:16:59.010 --> 00:17:01.320
H-He's really into it.

00:17:01.320 --> 00:17:05.620
Who would have thought there'd be a situation suited for his personality?

00:17:05.620 --> 00:17:12.240
He also has a chance to show off his legs by going outside.

00:17:12.780 --> 00:17:15.160
H-He's wearing pantyhose, isn't he?

00:17:15.160 --> 00:17:18.670
That's something we'll never have to experience in our lives,

00:17:18.670 --> 00:17:21.060
yet he's wearing it without a second thought.

00:17:21.060 --> 00:17:24.640
It makes it look even more suggestive, like some kind of fetish.

00:17:24.640 --> 00:17:28.050
Well, I shouldn't comment any further.

00:17:28.050 --> 00:17:29.610
Y-Yeah.

00:17:40.530 --> 00:17:42.240
Thank you very much!

00:17:43.370 --> 00:17:44.790
Two more to go!

00:17:46.120 --> 00:17:47.540
One left!

00:17:51.420 --> 00:17:53.270
We've sold everything!

00:17:53.840 --> 00:17:55.300
Congratulations!

00:17:55.300 --> 00:17:56.720
Thank you very much!

00:17:56.720 --> 00:17:58.140
Good work!

00:17:58.140 --> 00:18:00.050
Wow, really?

00:18:00.050 --> 00:18:03.530
Well, Kousaka-kun deserves most of the credit.

00:18:03.530 --> 00:18:06.310
This is all I'm capable of doing.

00:18:13.230 --> 00:18:14.060
Saki-chan!

00:18:15.800 --> 00:18:17.420
What do you think, Saki-chan?

00:18:28.290 --> 00:18:33.300
Geez, I haven't eaten or drunk anything. I'm lucky to be alive,

00:18:33.680 --> 00:18:36.830
but I feel wonderful!

00:18:50.520 --> 00:18:52.970
Oh, Yabusaki-san, t-that's...

00:18:52.970 --> 00:18:55.160
Is this the book from Genshiken?

00:18:55.160 --> 00:18:56.570
Uh, yeah.

00:19:00.200 --> 00:19:01.590
Wh-What is it?

00:19:02.480 --> 00:19:04.990
What? What did you mean by that?

00:19:05.310 --> 00:19:12.630
<i>With this announcement,
the sixty-sixth Comic Festival has come to an end.</i>

00:19:22.490 --> 00:19:25.240
Now that we're done cleaning, let's go.

00:19:25.240 --> 00:19:26.170
Yeah.

00:19:26.170 --> 00:19:28.530
We completely sold out.

00:19:28.530 --> 00:19:32.610
Yeah, by force... or should I say seduction?

00:19:33.610 --> 00:19:35.720
Oh, by the way, Sasahara.

00:19:35.720 --> 00:19:37.730
Did you buy the application form for the Winter Comifes?

00:19:37.730 --> 00:19:40.030
What's that?

00:19:40.030 --> 00:19:42.530
Oh, didn't you know?

00:19:42.530 --> 00:19:46.270
The application deadline for the
Winter Comifes is three days from now,

00:19:46.270 --> 00:19:50.920
so you need to purchase the form at
the information desk before you leave.

00:19:50.920 --> 00:19:52.270
Three days...

00:19:55.440 --> 00:19:57.750
It just ended right now, didn't it?

00:19:57.750 --> 00:20:02.170
That's true, but the winter Comifes is only four months away.

00:20:02.170 --> 00:20:04.680
Everyone does it in that cycle.

00:20:05.020 --> 00:20:09.670
We can buy the application form now and
decide whether we want to participate later.

00:20:09.670 --> 00:20:10.520
What do you say?

00:20:12.720 --> 00:20:14.230
What do you think, Kugayama-san?

00:20:14.230 --> 00:20:16.190
It's up to you, Sasahara.

00:20:17.750 --> 00:20:19.110
H-How about you, Ogiue-san?

00:20:19.110 --> 00:20:21.030
I'll leave it to you, Sasahara-senpai.

00:20:25.970 --> 00:20:28.080
Well, let's just go back for the time being.

00:20:28.080 --> 00:20:29.620
Oh, he ran away.

00:20:30.270 --> 00:20:33.850
We just finished,
and that's the last thing I want to think about right now.

00:20:33.850 --> 00:20:37.200
Everyone submits their applications without a second thought.

00:20:38.410 --> 00:20:41.000
Well, if you're asking me to do that again...

00:20:41.510 --> 00:20:43.470
I-It's not worth fighting over.

00:20:43.840 --> 00:20:45.890
Hey, wait a minute.

00:20:45.890 --> 00:20:49.110
Aren't you guys just leaving everything to Sasahara?

00:20:52.810 --> 00:20:56.960
83,500 yen, including expenses.

00:20:59.440 --> 00:21:00.690
I'm getting a headache.

00:21:05.820 --> 00:21:07.190
Isn't it great?

00:21:07.190 --> 00:21:08.330
Yeah...

00:21:08.330 --> 00:21:09.980
How was the cosplay?

00:21:09.980 --> 00:21:11.810
P-Pretty good, I guess.

00:21:11.810 --> 00:21:13.330
Wasn't it?

00:21:13.330 --> 00:21:17.270
Well, Kousaka is one of a kind.
That was something else.

00:21:17.910 --> 00:21:20.090
Geez, don't remind me about it.

00:22:55.010 --> 00:22:56.920
I'm telling you, Saki-san...

00:22:56.920 --> 00:22:59.360
Ohno, you're already drunk.

00:22:59.360 --> 00:23:00.810
I'm not drunk!

00:23:00.810 --> 00:23:02.840
I was talking about cosplaying
as the president!

00:23:06.080 --> 00:23:09.150
Most of it was spent on the celebration...

00:23:10.740 --> 00:23:13.720
T-Tanaka, w-what got you into it?

00:23:13.720 --> 00:23:17.300
I think it was when I saw my friend's
figurines. I was impressed with their quality.

00:23:17.300 --> 00:23:18.820
3-3D right from the beginning?

00:23:18.820 --> 00:23:20.100
Yeah. What about you?

00:23:20.100 --> 00:23:24.010
Y-Yeah, it was also through a friend. He brought a doujinshi to school.

00:23:24.010 --> 00:23:25.170
R-18 right from the beginning?

00:23:25.170 --> 00:23:29.270
W-W-Well, yeah. Do you still
keep in touch with him?

00:23:29.270 --> 00:23:31.440
He suddenly turned back to normal.

00:23:31.440 --> 00:23:38.060
Yeah, p-people who drag you into these kinds of hobbies are the f-first to grow out of them.

00:23:38.060 --> 00:23:39.510
Wh-Why is that?
